<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>BTA Admin DNS Tunneling</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
  </head>
  <body class="workspace-page">
    <main class="workspace-shell">
      <section class="hero-band">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Hypothesis 2 Proof</p>
          <h1>DNS Tunneling From Payment Terminals</h1>
          <p class="subtitle">
            Arm a compromised payment terminal here, then trigger the actual DNS burst from a live
            customer booking that uses the same terminal ID.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <nav class="page-nav">
            <a class="nav-link" href="/admin/dashboard">Admin Dashboard</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/admin/passenger/tickets">Fetch Tickets</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/admin/simulations/auth-sequence">Auth Sequence</a>
            <a class="nav-link active" href="/admin/simulations/dns-tunneling">DNS Tunneling</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/admin/simulations/payment-skimming">Payment Skimming</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/admin/simulations/gps-spoofing">GPS Spoofing</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/admin/simulations/ransomware">Ransomware</a>
          </nav>
          <form method="post" action="/logout">
            <button class="secondary" type="submit">Log Out</button>
          </form>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-layout">
        <article class="detail-card detail-card-wide">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Terminal Controls</p>
            <span class="status-pill warn">POST /api/simulations/dns-tunneling</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Payment Terminal DNS Burst</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">
            This console exists specifically to prove Hypothesis 2. First arm the terminal profile
            here. Then open the customer booking page in another session and submit a booking with
            the same terminal ID to generate the long TXT-style queries.
          </p>

          <form
            class="detail-form"
            method="post"
            action="/api/simulations/dns-tunneling"
            data-console-form="dns-tunneling"
          >
            <div class="form-grid">
              <label>
                <span>Simulation Secret</span>
                <input type="text" name="simulation_secret" value="<%= simulationSecret %>" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Terminal ID</span>
                <input type="text" name="terminal_id" value="A01-PAY-014" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Terminal Site</span>
                <input type="text" name="terminal_site" value="Majestic Gate 2" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Network Segment</span>
                <input type="text" name="terminal_segment" value="payment-vlan" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Malicious Domain</span>
                <input type="text" name="malicious_domain" value="attacker-domain.com" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Query Count</span>
                <input type="number" name="query_count" min="1" max="100" value="12" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Random Label Length</span>
                <input type="number" name="label_length" min="32" max="180" value="104" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Query Type</span>
                <select name="query_type">
                  <option value="TXT">TXT</option>
                  <option value="NULL">NULL</option>
                  <option value="CNAME">CNAME</option>
                </select>
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Query Interval (ms)</span>
                <input type="number" name="query_interval_ms" min="0" max="5000" value="40" />
              </label>
            </div>
            <label>
              <span>Operator Note</span>
              <textarea name="operator_note" rows="4">High-volume TXT query drill for payment-terminal exfiltration hunting.</textarea>
            </label>
            <div class="form-actions">
              <button type="submit">Arm DNS Tunneling</button>
              <a class="ghost-link" href="/admin/dashboard">Back To Dashboard</a>
            </div>
          </form>
        </article>

        <article class="detail-card">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Expected Events</p>
            <span class="status-pill success">Graylog Ready</span>
          </div>
          <h2>What Will Be Emitted</h2>
          <ul class="detail-list">
            <li>Arming emits `message:dns_tunneling_armed` with the selected terminal metadata.</li>
            <li>The matching customer booking emits `message:dns_tunneling_suspected` events with long labels.</li>
            <li>Use the same terminal ID on both pages to prove the payment-terminal exfiltration path.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="chip-wrap">
            <span class="data-chip">message:dns_tunneling_armed</span>
            <span class="data-chip">message:dns_tunneling_suspected</span>
            <span class="data-chip">terminal_id</span>
            <span class="data-chip">protocol:DNS</span>
            <span class="data-chip">query_length</span>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-layout">
        <article class="detail-card detail-card-wide">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Run Summary</p>
            <span class="status-pill neutral">API Response</span>
          </div>
          <div id="simulation-summary" class="result-empty">
            Arm the terminal to see the accepted profile, then complete a matching customer booking
            to generate the DNS logs.
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="detail-card">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Raw API Body</p>
            <span class="status-pill neutral">JSON</span>
          </div>
          <pre id="console-response" class="response-pre">Run the console to inspect the response body.</pre>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>
    <script src="/console.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
